1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,923
Your AI agent just used 287,000 tokens.

2
00:00:04,923 --> 00:00:05,498
On what?

3
00:00:06,183 --> 00:00:08,892
Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, OpenCode.

4
00:00:08,892 --> 00:00:12,626
Four agents, four log formats, and zero visibility.

5
00:00:13,317 --> 00:00:14,911
Meet Know Your Tokens:

6
00:00:14,911 --> 00:00:18,245
one local dashboard for every AI coding agent.

7
00:00:18,983 --> 00:00:20,952
Exact tokens for every request.

8
00:00:20,952 --> 00:00:22,031
Debug any prompt.

9
00:00:22,031 --> 00:00:24,381
And everything stays on your machine.

10
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:27,665
Getting started takes one command.

11
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:30,068
Run npx knowyourtokens.

12
00:00:30,068 --> 00:00:36,051
It sets up a private environment, wires the hooks, finds your agents, and opens the dashboard.

13
00:00:37,917 --> 00:00:39,580
This is your command center.

14
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:44,095
Total tokens, input, output and cache, with a daily trend and the token mix.

15
00:00:44,095 --> 00:00:47,005
Cache reads usually dominate, and that's healthy:

16
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:49,797
reused context costs a fraction of fresh input.

17
00:00:49,797 --> 00:00:52,530
Change the date range, and every card follows.

18
00:00:55,883 --> 00:01:02,091
The Agents page puts every agent side by side, including anything you push through the API.

19
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:06,667
Requests lists every model call with its exact tokens.

20
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:09,654
Click one to see its model, agent and prompt.

21
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:12,080
Here's the real power.

22
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:15,769
This request used almost 288,000 tokens.

23
00:01:15,769 --> 00:01:20,073
The breakdown shows where they went, and the full prompt reveals the culprit:

24
00:01:20,073 --> 00:01:22,141
a whole log file pasted into context.

25
00:01:22,141 --> 00:01:25,271
Trim it, and the next request is a fraction of the size.

26
00:01:25,983 --> 00:01:32,127
Projects show which sessions and requests use the most context, so you know exactly where to optimize.

27
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:42,162
See every tool call, skill and MCP server your agents use, and every session with its requests and tokens.

28
00:01:45,317 --> 00:01:54,213
Before you paste something big, the token calculator estimates it offline, shows how much of the context window it takes, and prices it at your own rates.

29
00:01:57,850 --> 00:02:04,719
Export everything as CSV, JSON or NDJSON, or build on the REST API and SDKs.

30
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:08,678
Using Antigravity, Cursor, or your own agent?

31
00:02:08,678 --> 00:02:11,070
Push one JSON record per request.

32
00:02:11,783 --> 00:02:12,906
Every agent in.

33
00:02:12,906 --> 00:02:14,029
Every tool out.

34
00:02:14,029 --> 00:02:15,901
All local, and all yours.

35
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:21,135
Know Your Tokens is free and open source.

36
00:02:21,135 --> 00:02:25,006
Run npx knowyourtokens, and give it a star on GitHub.

37
00:02:26,883 --> 00:02:28,642
Built by Sarvesh Talele.

38
00:02:28,642 --> 00:02:31,427
Follow for more AI engineering builds.
